    "body": "The 1.25 assembly is quite funny and goes in a round about way, it's taking the inverse of an inverse to move stuff around from flags to GP.\nI think we should be able to do:\n```\nADDQ  CX, DX\nADCQ  SI, BX\nADCQ  $0, AX\n```\nor something like that\nwhich is what I was trying to do before giving up (I only thought about using the carry flag from a compare which is almost always pointless since there is only unsigned `x < y` which generate the correct condition in the carry flag.)",
