    "body": "**Related Issues**\n\n - [cmd/compile: amd64 carry flag spilling uses SBBQ + NEGQ instead of SETCS #68961](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/68961) <!-- score=0.89000 -->\n - [cmd/compile: on \\`AMD64\\` slow instruction sequence to Zext a \\< register size instruction output #76066](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/76066) <!-- score=0.84506 -->\n - [cmd/compile: performance regression on ppc64 due to change in scheduling CL 270940 #57976 (closed)](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/57976) <!-- score=0.84428 -->\n - [cmd/compile: ARM64 CSE flags generation between \\`CMP 0$\\` and instruction already setting the flags according to the result #74878](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74878) <!-- score=0.83540 -->\n - [cmd/compile: suboptimal code generation for bit test (regression in Go 1.15) #44228 (closed)](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/44228) <!-- score=0.83214 -->\n - [cmd/compile: suboptimal arm64 output #43145](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/43145) <!-- score=0.83122 -->\n - [cmd/compile: performance regression compiling crypto/internal/edwards25519/field.feMulGeneric on PPC64 #56497 (closed)](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/56497) <!-- score=0.82872 -->\n\n**Related Code Changes**\n\n - [cmd/compile: schedule carry chain arithmetic disjointly](https://go-review.googlesource.com/c/go/+/393656#related-content) <!-- score=0.84475 -->\n - [cmd/compile: enable carry chain scheduling for arm64](https://go-review.googlesource.com/c/go/+/424907#related-content) <!-- score=0.84253 -->\n - [cmd/compile: intrinsify math/bits.Sub on amd64](https://go-review.googlesource.com/c/go/+/144258#related-content) <!-- score=0.83091 -->\n\n<sub>(Emoji vote if this was helpful or unhelpful; more detailed feedback welcome in [this discussion](https://github.com/golang/go/discussions/67901).)</sub>\n",
